    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The queue is a first-in-first-out (FIFO) data structure."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "A queue data structure is similar to a queue in real life. Suppose you're in line at a movie theater."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Queue in Ticket Counter",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The first person in the line will be the first to get a ticket, and the last person in the line is last to get the tickets. This is the concept of FIFO."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "In computer science, a queue is used to maintain a particular order of operations, like managing processes in an operating system and handling requests on a web server."
    },
